BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 758 Tm (RELATIVITY: THE SPECIAL AND GENERAL THEORY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 738 Tm (Of course the conviction of the "truth" of geometrical propositions in this sense is founded) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 725.5 Tm (exclusively on rather incomplete experience. For the present we shall assume the "truth" of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 713 Tm (the geometrical propositions, then at a later stage \(in the general theory of relativity\) we) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700.5 Tm (shall see that this "truth" is limited, and we shall consider the extent of its limitation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 675.5 Tm (II. The System of Co-ordinates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 650.5 Tm (On the basis of the physical interpretation of distance which has been indicated, we are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 638 Tm (also in a position to establish the distance between two points on a rigid body by means of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 625.5 Tm (measurements. For this purpose we require a "distance" \(rod S\) which is to be used once and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 613 Tm (for all, and which we employ as a standard measure. If, now, A and B are two points on a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 600.5 Tm (rigid body, we can construct the line joining them according to the rules of geometry; then,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 588 Tm (starting from A, we can mark off the distance S time after time until we reach B. The number) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 575.5 Tm (of these operations required is the numerical measure of the distance AB. This is the basis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 563 Tm (of all measurement of length.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 538 Tm (Every description of the scene of an event or of the position of an object in space is based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 525.5 Tm (on the specification of the point on a rigid body \(body of reference\) with which that event) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 513 Tm (or object coincides. This applies not only to scientific description, but also to everyday) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 500.5 Tm (life. If I analyse the place specification "Trafalgar Square, London" I arrive at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 488 Tm (following result. The earth is the rigid body to which the specification of place refers;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 475.5 Tm ("Trafalgar Square, London" is a well-defined point, to which a name has been assigned, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 463 Tm (with which the event coincides in space.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 438 Tm (I have chosen this as being more familiar to the English reader than the "Potzdammer Platz,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 425.5 Tm (Berlin," which is referred to in the original. \(R. W. L.\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 400.5 Tm (This primitive method of place specification deals only with places on the surface of rigid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 388 Tm (bodies, and is dependent on the existence of points on this surface which are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 375.5 Tm (distinguishable from each other. But we can free ourselves from both of these limitations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 363 Tm (without altering the nature of our specification of position. If, for instance, a cloud is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 350.5 Tm (hovering over Trafalgar Square, then we can determine its position relative to the surface) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 338 Tm (of the earth by erecting a pole perpendicularly on the Square, so that it reaches the cloud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 325.5 Tm (The length of the pole measured with the standard measuring-rod, combined with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 313 Tm (specification of the position of the foot of the pole, supplies us with a complete place) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 300.5 Tm (specification. On the basis of this illustration, we are able to see the manner in which a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 288 Tm (refinement of the conception of position has been developed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 263 Tm (\(a\) We imagine the rigid body, to which the place specification is referred, supplemented in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 250.5 Tm (such a manner that the object whose position we require is reached by the completed rigid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 238 Tm (body.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 213 Tm (\(b\) In locating the position of the object, we make use of a number \(here the length of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 200.5 Tm (pole measured with the measuring-rod\) instead of designated points of reference.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 175.5 Tm (\(c\) We speak of the height of the cloud even when the pole which reaches the cloud has not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 163 Tm (been erected. By means of optical observations of the cloud from different positions on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 150.5 Tm (ground, and taking into account the properties of the propagation of light, we determine the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 138 Tm (length of the pole we should have required in order to reach the cloud.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 113 Tm (From this consideration we see that it will be advantageous if, in the description of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 100.5 Tm (position, it should be possible by means of numerical measures to make ourselves independent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 88 Tm (of the existence of marked positions \(possessing names\) on the rigid body of reference. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 295 40 Tm (- 2 -) Tj ET
