BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 588 Tm (following method suggests itself. If we call A' and B' the two points on the train whose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 575.5 Tm (distance apart is required, then both of these points are moving with the velocity v along) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 563 Tm (the embankment. In the first place we require to determine the points A and B of the) Tj ET
