BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 650.5 Tm (Thus the body has the same energy as a body of mass) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 625.5 Tm (moving with the velocity v. Hence we can say: If a body takes up an amount of energy E0,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 613 Tm (then its inertial mass increases by an amount) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 588 Tm (the inertial mass of a body is not a constant but varies according to the change in the) Tj ET
