BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 563 Tm (measure of its energy. The law of the conservation of the mass of a system becomes identical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 550.5 Tm (with the law of the conservation of energy, and is only valid provided that the system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 538 Tm (neither takes up nor sends out energy. Writing the expression for the energy in the form) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 513 Tm (we see that the term mc2, which has hitherto attracted our attention, is nothing else than) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 500.5 Tm (the energy possessed by the body before it absorbed the energy E0.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 475.5 Tm (A direct comparison of this relation with experiment is not possible at the present time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 463 Tm (\(1920; see[Note], p. 48\), owing to the fact that the changes in energy E0 to which we can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 450.5 Tm (subject a system are not large enough to make themselves perceptible as a change in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 438 Tm (inertial mass of the system.) Tj ET
