BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 500.5 Tm (with reference to the ther, this time T' is different when the body is moving) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 488 Tm (perpendicularly to the planes of the mirrors from that resulting when the motion is parallel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 475.5 Tm (to these planes. Although the estimated difference between these two times is exceedingly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 463 Tm (small, Michelson and Morley performed an experiment involving interference in which this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 450.5 Tm (difference should have been clearly detectable. But the experiment gave a negative result--a) Tj ET
