BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 375.5 Tm (this solution of the difficulty was the right one. But on the basis of the theory of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 363 Tm (relativity the method of interpretation is incomparably more satisfactory. According to this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 350.5 Tm (theory there is no such thing as a "specially favoured" \(unique\) co-ordinate system to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 338 Tm (occasion the introduction of the ther-idea, and hence there can be no ther-drift, nor any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 325.5 Tm (experiment with which to demonstrate it. Here the contraction of moving bodies follows from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 313 Tm (the two fundamental principles of the theory, without the introduction of particular) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 300.5 Tm (hypotheses; and as the prime factor involved in this contraction we find, not the motion in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 288 Tm (itself, to which we cannot attach any meaning, but the motion with respect to the body of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 275.5 Tm (reference chosen in the particular case in point. Thus for a co-ordinate system moving with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 263 Tm (the earth the mirror system of Michelson and Morley is not shortened, but it is shortened) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 250.5 Tm (for a co-ordinate system which is at rest relatively to the sun.) Tj ET
