BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 758 Tm (RELATIVITY: THE SPECIAL AND GENERAL THEORY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 738 Tm (The basal principle, which was the pivot of all our previous considerations, was the special) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 725.5 Tm (principle of relativity, i.e. the principle of the physical relativity of all uniform) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 713 Tm (motion. Let as once more analyse its meaning carefully.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 688 Tm (It was at all times clear that, from the point of view of the idea it conveys to us, every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 675.5 Tm (motion must be considered only as a relative motion. Returning to the illustration we have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 663 Tm (frequently used of the embankment and the railway carriage, we can express the fact of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 650.5 Tm (motion here taking place in the following two forms, both of which are equally justifiable:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 625.5 Tm (\(a\) The carriage is in motion relative to the embankment,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 600.5 Tm (\(b\) The embankment is in motion relative to the carriage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 575.5 Tm (In \(a\) the embankment, in \(b\) the carriage, serves as the body of reference in our statement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 563 Tm (of the motion taking place. If it is simply a question of detecting or of describing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 550.5 Tm (motion involved, it is in principle immaterial to what reference-body we refer the motion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 538 Tm (As already mentioned, this is self-evident, but it must not be confused with the much more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 525.5 Tm (comprehensive statement called "the principle of relativity," which we have taken as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 513 Tm (basis of our investigations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 488 Tm (The principle we have made use of not only maintains that we may equally well choose the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 475.5 Tm (carriage or the embankment as our reference-body for the description of any event \(for this,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 463 Tm (too, is self-evident\). Our principle rather asserts what follows: If we formulate the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 450.5 Tm (general laws of nature as they are obtained from experience, by making use of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 425.5 Tm (\(a\) the embankment as reference-body,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 400.5 Tm (\(b\) the railway carriage as reference-body,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 375.5 Tm (then these general laws of nature \(e.g. the laws of mechanics or the law of the propagation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 363 Tm (of light in vacuo\) have exactly the same form in both cases. This can also be expressed as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 350.5 Tm (follows: For the physical description of natural processes, neither of the reference bodies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 338 Tm (K, K' is unique \(lit. "specially marked out"\) as compared with the other. Unlike the first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 325.5 Tm (this latter statement need not of necessity hold a priori; it is not contained in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 313 Tm (conceptions of "motion" and "reference-body" and derivable from them; only experience can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 300.5 Tm (decide as to its correctness or incorrectness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 275.5 Tm (Up to the present, however, we have by no means maintained the equivalence of all bodies of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 263 Tm (reference K in connection with the formulation of natural laws. Our course was more on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 250.5 Tm (following Iines. In the first place, we started out from the assumption that there exists a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 238 Tm (reference-body K, whose condition of motion is such that the Galileian law holds with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 225.5 Tm (respect to it: A particle left to itself and sufficiently far removed from all other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 213 Tm (particles moves uniformly in a straight line. With reference to K \(Galileian reference-body\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 200.5 Tm (the laws of nature were to be as simple as possible. But in addition to K, all bodies of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 188 Tm (reference K' should be given preference in this sense, and they should be exactly equivalent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 175.5 Tm (to K for the formulation of natural laws, provided that they are in a state of uniform) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 163 Tm (rectilinear and non-rotary motion with respect to K; all these bodies of reference are to be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 150.5 Tm (regarded as Galileian reference-bodies. The validity of the principle of relativity was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 138 Tm (assumed only for these reference-bodies, but not for others \(e.g. those possessing motion of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 125.5 Tm (a different kind\). In this sense we speak of the special principle of relativity, or special) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 113 Tm (theory of relativity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 88 Tm (In contrast to this we wish to understand by the "general principle of relativity" the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 292.8 40 Tm (- 20 -) Tj ET
