BT /F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 758 Tm (RELATIVITY: THE SPECIAL AND GENERAL THEORY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 738 Tm (following statement: All bodies of reference K, K', etc., are equivalent for the description) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 725.5 Tm (of natural phenomena \(formulation of the general laws of nature\), whatever may be their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 713 Tm (state of motion. But before proceeding farther, it ought to be pointed out that this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700.5 Tm (formulation must be replaced later by a more abstract one, for reasons which will become) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 688 Tm (evident at a later stage.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 663 Tm (Since the introduction of the special principle of relativity has been justified, every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 650.5 Tm (intellect which strives after generalisation must feel the temptation to venture the step) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 638 Tm (towards the general principle of relativity. But a simple and apparently quite reliable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 625.5 Tm (consideration seems to suggest that, for the present at any rate, there is little hope of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 613 Tm (success in such an attempt; Let us imagine ourselves transferred to our old friend the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 600.5 Tm (railway carriage, which is travelling at a uniform rate. As long as it is moving uniformly,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 588 Tm (the occupant of the carriage is not sensible of its motion, and it is for this reason that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 575.5 Tm (he can without reluctance interpret the facts of the case as indicating that the carriage is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 563 Tm (at rest, but the embankment in motion. Moreover, according to the special principle of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 550.5 Tm (relativity, this interpretation is quite justified also from a physical point of view. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 538 Tm (the motion of the carriage is now changed into a non-uniform motion, as for instance by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 525.5 Tm (powerful application of the brakes, then the occupant of the carriage experiences a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 513 Tm (correspondingly powerful jerk forwards. The retarded motion is manifested in the mechanical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 500.5 Tm (behaviour of bodies relative to the person in the railway carriage. The mechanical behaviour) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 488 Tm (is different from that of the case previously considered, and for this reason it would) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 475.5 Tm (appear to be impossible that the same mechanical laws hold relatively to the non-uniformly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 463 Tm (moving carriage, as hold with reference to the carriage when at rest or in uniform motion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 450.5 Tm (At all events it is clear that the Galileian law does not hold with respect to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 438 Tm (non-uniformly moving carriage. Because of this, we feel compelled at the present juncture to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 425.5 Tm (grant a kind of absolute physical reality to non-uniform motion, in opposition to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 413 Tm (general principle of relativity. But in what follows we shall soon see that this conclusion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 400.5 Tm (cannot be maintained.) Tj ET
